From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] platform: arm64: huawei-gaokun-ec: report the real lid state on resume

gaokun_ec_resume() reports the lid as open on every resume, whatever woke the
system. With the lid closed, the first resume from any other source, even an
aborted suspend, looks like the lid opening. Android answers with
WAKE_REASON_LID: the screen comes on with the cover closed, and the lid counts
as open until it is next opened and closed.

Read EC_LID_STATE, as the IRQ handler and the probe path do, and report that.
The read comes before the IRQ is enabled again, so a pending EC_EVENT_LID is
handled afterwards and only reports a difference. If the read fails, keep the
last state: Android acts only on a change, so a failed read neither wakes a
closed tablet nor puts one in use to sleep.

The IRQ handler ignores the result of the same read, and on failure compares
an uninitialized status. Android now acts on the lid, so skip the event then.

Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 drivers/platform/arm64/huawei-gaokun-ec.c | 19 ++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/platform/arm64/huawei-gaokun-ec.c b/drivers/platform/arm64/huawei-gaokun-ec.c
--- a/drivers/platform/arm64/huawei-gaokun-ec.c
+++ b/drivers/platform/arm64/huawei-gaokun-ec.c
@@ -658,6 +658,7 @@ static int gaokun_ec_resume(struct device *dev)
 {
 	struct gaokun_ec *ec = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
 	u8 ec_req[] = MKREQ(0x02, EC_STANDBY_REG, 1, EC_STANDBY_EXIT);
+	u8 status;
 	int ret;
 	int i;
 
@@ -678,10 +679,16 @@ static int gaokun_ec_resume(struct device *dev)
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
-	/* Resume may be unstable, so open lid anyways */
-	input_report_switch(ec->idev, SW_LID, 0);
-	input_sync(ec->idev);
-	ec->lid_opened = true;
+	/*
+	 * Any wakeup source ends up here, so report the lid as the EC sees it:
+	 * a wakeup with the lid closed must not look like the lid opening.
+	 * If the read fails, keep the last state.
+	 */
+	if (!gaokun_ec_psy_read_byte(ec, EC_LID_STATE, &status)) {
+		ec->lid_opened = status & EC_LID_OPEN;
+		input_report_switch(ec->idev, SW_LID, !ec->lid_opened);
+		input_sync(ec->idev);
+	}
 
 	ec->suspended = false;
 	enable_irq(ec->client->irq);
@@ -758,7 +765,9 @@ static irqreturn_t gaokun_ec_irq_handler(int irq, void *data)
 		break;
 
 	case EC_EVENT_LID:
-		gaokun_ec_psy_read_byte(ec, EC_LID_STATE, &status);
+		if (gaokun_ec_psy_read_byte(ec, EC_LID_STATE, &status))
+			break;
+
 		status &= EC_LID_OPEN;
 		if (ec->lid_opened != !!status) {
 			input_report_switch(ec->idev, SW_LID, !status);
